-- Game Pack 2: freeware/public-domain classics with modern runners (ScummVM adventures, ZZT + Zeta,
-- Scorched Earth, Abuse, Liero). Linked files: ext_url points at each official download, streamed via /dl/.
INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (2, 'GAMES2.NFO', 'READ ME FIRST: Game Pack 2, what runs what', 4285, 'SysOp', 1792630000100, 'approved', 1, '==============================================================================
       G A M E   P A C K   2   ::   more classics, legal and free
==============================================================================
 Every one of these was made free by the people who own it: released as
 freeware, put in the public domain, or given away by the author. All the
 files come straight from the official homes listed below, untouched.
 All downloads are FREE (no ratio hit).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SCUMMVM ADVENTURES          SCUMMVM-WIN.ZIP / SCUMMVM-MAC.DMG + the games
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ScummVM (GNU GPL) runs the old point-and-click adventures on modern Macs
 and PCs. Get ScummVM for your machine, unzip a game into its own folder,
 then in ScummVM click Add Game... and pick that folder. These are the
 freeware games ScummVM itself hands out, by permission of their owners:

   BASS-CD.ZIP ......... Beneath a Steel Sky (1994), the full CD talkie
   LURE.ZIP ............ Lure of the Temptress (1992)
   FOTAQ.ZIP ........... Flight of the Amazon Queen (1995), talkie
   DRASCULA.ZIP ........ Drascula: The Vampire Strikes Back (1996)
   DRASCULA-AUDIO.ZIP .. Drascula''s CD music, unzip it into the same folder
   DREAMWEB.ZIP ........ DreamWeb (1994), cyberpunk noir. Grown-up themes.
   NIPPON.ZIP .......... Nippon Safes, Inc. (1992)
   SOLTYS.ZIP .......... Soltys (1995)
   SFINX.ZIP ........... Sfinx (1997)
   GODTHUND.ZIP ........ God of Thunder (1993), Norse action-adventure
   MYSTHOUS.ZIP ........ Mystery House (1980), Sierra''s very first game

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ZZT                          ZZT32.ZIP + ZETA-WIN.ZIP / ZETA-MAC.ZIP
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Tim Sweeney''s ZZT (1991), the game that started Epic MegaGames, with all
 four original worlds. Epic re-licensed it in 1997 so it can be passed
 around free. Zeta (MIT license) runs it on modern machines: unzip both,
 then open ZZT.EXE with Zeta (or drop the ZZT folder on it).
 From the Museum of ZZT (museumofzzt.com) and zeta.asie.pl.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 DOS CLASSICS (run them in DOSBox Staging, see TOOLS.NFO)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SCORCH15.ZIP ..... Scorched Earth 1.5 (1995), "The Mother of All Games".
                    Wendell Hicken gives it away free on whicken.com (you
                    can tip him there for the Totally Scorched collection).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 WINDOWS-ONLY PORTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ABUSE-WIN.ZIP .... Abuse (1996), Crack dot Com''s run-and-gun. The code and
                    data were put in the public domain; this port is by
                    Xenoveritas (github.com/Xenoveritas/abuse). The original
                    sound effects aren''t included (see the port''s readme).
 LIERO.ZIP ........ Liero 1.36 (1998), the worm deathmatch, with OpenLiero.
                    Freeware by Joosa Riekkinen, now under the WTFPL.
                    From github.com/gliptic/liero.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 MAC USERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The first time you open ScummVM or Zeta, macOS may refuse. Right-click the
 app, choose Open, then Open again (or System Settings > Privacy & Security
 > Open Anyway).

 Credits: Revolution Software (Beneath a Steel Sky, Lure of the
 Temptress), Interactive Binary Illusions (Flight of the Amazon Queen),
 Alcachofa Soft (Drascula), Creative Reality (DreamWeb), Euclidea (Nippon
 Safes), LK Avalon (Soltys, Sfinx), Ron Davis / Adept Software (God of
 Thunder), Sierra On-Line (Mystery House), Tim Sweeney / Epic (ZZT),
 Wendell Hicken (Scorched Earth), Crack dot Com (Abuse), Joosa Riekkinen
 (Liero). And the ScummVM team, who made all of this playable again.
==============================================================================
', 'text/plain');
